{"title":"Count The Number Of Powerful Integers","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given three integers start, finish, and limit. You are also given a 0-indexed string s representing a positive integer.\nA positive integer x is called powerful if it ends with s (in other words, s is a suffix of x) and each digit in x is at most limit.\nReturn the total number of powerful integers in the range [start..finish].\nA string x is a suffix of a string y if and only if x is a substring of y that starts from some index (including 0) in y and extends to the index y.length - 1. For example, 25 is a suffix of 5125 whereas 512 is not.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: start = 1, finish = 6000, limit = 4, s = \"124\"\nOutput: 5\n```\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: start = 15, finish = 215, limit = 6, s = \"10\"\nOutput: 2\n```\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: start = 1000, finish = 2000, limit = 4, s = \"3000\"\nOutput: 0\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= start <= finish <= 10^15\n- 1 <= limit <= 9\n- 1 <= s.length <= floor(log10(finish)) + 1\n- s only consists of numeric digits which are at most limit.\n- s does not have leading zeros.\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def numberOfPowerfulInt(self, start: int, finish: int, limit: int, s: str) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().numberOfPowerfulInt","parameters":[{"name":"start","type":"int"},{"name":"finish","type":"int"},{"name":"limit","type":"int"},{"name":"s","type":"str"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[1,1000000000000000,9,"1"],"expected":100000000000000},{"input":[1,10892521561083,7,"71215"],"expected":18874368},{"input":[1,112240704540373,8,"36268056442178"],"expected":1},{"input":[1,112800918794137,5,"45002302154552"],"expected":1},{"input":[1,114,8,"261"],"expected":0},{"input":[1,115651620352408,9,"3"],"expected":11565162035241},{"input":[1,116,6,"1"],"expected":9},{"input":[1,119107643423806,1,"11111"],"expected":1024},{"input":[1,120752808294460,4,"34040334211"